    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102-a1">

                <pb facs="0395" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg347"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram per cable.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Johnson</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 25, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Inform Webb at Rio that instructions to him were sent yesterday by United States
                    mail steamship from New York to Rio. His demand for permission for the Wasp to
                    go for Washburn is approved, but his demand for passport must be suspended until
                    further directions, which will go by the same mail steamer, September 23d.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reverdy Johnson,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
